  "description": "Native .NET document layout analysis: detect and classify page regions (title, text, table, figure, caption, formula, header/footer…), order them the way a human reads, and optionally OCR text regions through a pluggable recognizer — all on ONNX Runtime, no Python required.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "LayoutSharp",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-08-29T16:29:23.103Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "QzDoBJZ1m3qq/JjnZUulRyV7WL3dRQ44QE3TK5J1E0LGb/5tviVbDL/yFO/omDE4yY0BpAjiKtT+wQNE5gop0g==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 286267,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/FarhanLodi/LayoutSharp",
  "published": "2026-08-29T16:26:48.487Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0: first release. Native .NET document layout analysis on ONNX Runtime — detects and classifies page regions (title, section header, text, list, table, figure, caption, formula, footnote, header/footer, page number, seal, checkbox, form, key-value region) with a choice of two Apache-2.0 detectors, checksum-verified download on first use: PP-DocLayoutV3 (default, 25 classes, the one that detects seals, charts and vertical CJK text) and Docling heron (17 classes, faster, adds list/checkbox/form/key-value). Orders regions with XY-cut reading order (or the detector's own), and returns a typed Document → Page → Block graph with JSON, plain-text and Markdown export. Text recognition is pluggable via ITextRecognizer (bring your own OCR — EasyOcrSharp, Tesseract, a cloud API — or run layout-only). Runtime dependencies: Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime, EasyImageSharp (MIT, fully managed — no native image codecs) and the Microsoft.Extensions DI/logging abstractions. No Python required.",
